+
+    `CliRunner` cannot be used here: it captures output into a buffer that
+    cannot fail, and the whole subject is a write that does. `/dev/full` is a
+    real stream whose every write returns ENOSPC, line buffered so the failure
+    lands inside the command rather than at interpreter shutdown.
